adjudication.rationale:
In `ClientPermissionsV2.hasPermission(ClientModel client, String scope)`, the fallback to evaluating the realm-wide “all-clients” resource only happens when the per-client resource is `null`:

```java
Resource resource = resourceStore.findByName(server, client.getId(), server.getId());
if (resource == null) {
  resource = ...getResourceTypeResource(...CLIENTS_RESOURCE_TYPE);
  if (policyStore.findByResource(server, resource).isEmpty()) return false;
}
Collection<Permission> permissions = root.evaluatePermission(new ResourcePermission(resource, ...));
```

If a per-client `Resource` exists but has no policies attached, the code evaluates permissions against that empty-policy per-client resource and never evaluates the all-clients resource, so an existing all-clients grant won’t be seen. This matches the advisory: the `findByResource(...).isEmpty()` guard is only in the `resource == null` branch, and there is no alternate path to try the all-clients resource when the per-client resource is present but effectively unconfigured.
